# LAWS 2 AND 3, THE PERMIT, in the form affine-kinds decision 001 gives (note/project/term/affine-kinds/decision/
# 001-many-by-default-sole-and-hide-declared-per-form.md). They hold by construction, not by a claim:
#
#   no forged permit       `mark hide`: only model.tree makes a permit, so the one way to get one is `grant-delete`
#   every mutating route   the one public mutator here, `delete-note`, takes a permit for the note it erases, and
#   asks                   the mutator under it, `bury-at`, is `mark private`. The event log's one erase, model.tree's
#                          `erase-of`, takes a permit too. `mark sole`: a permit is spent once
#
# ENFORCED since 2026-10-21: a route in another file that makes its own permit is refused as `hidden-make`
# (check/hide.ts, ../../twin/no-forged-permit), one that spends a permit twice as `sole-reused` (check/sole.ts,
# ../../twin/permit-reused), and one that skips the permit by calling the private mutator as `private-name`
# (check/private.ts, ../../twin/route-skips-permit).
#
# The permit and its one maker, `grant-delete`, live in model.tree beside `event`, since the one erase event
# (`erase-of`) is made there from a permit.
load ./model
  find natural
  find person
  find note
  find shelf
  find flag
  find same
  find permit

# THE MUTATING TASK takes the permit and nothing that names the target, so a permit for one note cannot erase another
task delete-note
  take s, like shelf
  take permit, like permit
  like shelf
  back
    bury-at
      read s
      read permit/note
      read permit/person

# bury the live note `at`, by `by`, with no check of its own: the permit was the check
task bury-at
  mark private
  take s, like shelf
  take at, like natural
  take by, like person
  like shelf
  sift s
    case bare
      back make bare
    case more
      back
        make more
          bind top, bury-one(top, at, by)
          bind rest, bury-at(rest, at, by)

task bury-one
  mark private
  take n, like note
  take aim, like natural
  take by, like person
  like note
  sift n
    case live
      back bury-if(same(at, aim), n, by)
    case gone
      back n

task bury-if
  mark private
  take f, like flag
  take n, like note
  take by, like person
  like note
  sift f
    case yes
      sift n
        case live
          back
            make gone
              bind at, at
              bind whose, whose
              bind by, by
        case gone
          back n
    case no
      back n
